/islandora/object/ailla%3A134134"}, {"title": "journalpub.escholarship.org", "url": "https://journalpub.escholarship.org/lucero/article/53591/galley/40500/download"}, {"title": "testsite2-do-notuse-or-register-here.nuestrosranchos.org", "url": "https://testsite2-do-notuse-or-register-here.nuestrosranchos.org/node/24528"}, {"title": "MunozJ Intro VidaVulgar v2", "url": "https://celacp.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/MunozJ-Intro-VidaVulgar-v2.pdf"}, {"title": "Diaz-De Leon family", "url": "https://mail.nuestrosranchos.org/node/24528"}]}, "The search didn't turn up anything linking José Luis de León Díaz to a novel called *San Pascualito*. The results cover a different author, the Guatemalan writer known as Luis de Lión, and his known work.\n\n- **Identity:** Luis de Lión is the pen name of José Luis de León Díaz, who was born in the Kaqchikel village of San Juan del Obispo, Sacatepéquez, Guatemala.\n- **Best-known novel:** El tiempo principia en Xibalbá, which won the Central American novel prize at the Juegos Florales at Quetzaltenango in 1972. It was not published, however, until 1985, after Lión's death.\n- **Dates:** A historical marker gives his birth as August 19, 1939 in San Juan del Obispo. Another source says he was a Guatemalan writer kidnapped on May 15, 1984 by elements of intelligence, and gives his death as 6 June 1984.\n\nThe results don't mention *San Pascualito*, so I can't confirm that title is his. The title may be a different work, a misremembered name, or simply absent from these sources. A search on the title alone, or on Luis de Lión's bibliography, would be the next step."], "durationSeconds": 4.897970125, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_017ZXXRwmzmgYNKNMPGEyVpU", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
